        "biography": "",
        "appearance": "",
        "notes": "<h5>Tactics</h5><p>A <strong>socialite</strong> shines in conversations, where their Charming Personality feature allows them to maintain composure while wearing down their opponents’ focus, and their Down the Grapevine reaction gains them further social leverage. Socialites aren’t likely to engage in combat unless forced, and when they must, they prioritize fleeing to safety. When cornered, they use their Beguiling Influence and Distracting Countenance actions to weaken foes (hoping for stronger allies to help finish them off), finally leaning on their Knife attack only as a last resort.</p>",
        "role": "rival"
    },
